'''Tiplar''' was a [[Color|yellow]]-skinned [[Mikkian]] [[Gender|female]] [[Jedi Master]] who served as a [[Jedi General]] within the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. As part of her military service, Tiplar and her [[twin]] sister [[Tiplee]] led a [[Doom's unit|unit]] of [[clone trooper]]s along with [[Clone Commander]] [[Doom]]. Such was the case during the [[Battle of Ringo Vinda]], in which the three of them collaborated with [[Jedi]] [[General]] [[Anakin Skywalker]]'s [[501st Legion]] to oust the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] from a [[Ringo Vinda space station|space station]] [[orbit]]ing [[Ringo Vinda]]. At the height of the campaign, 501st [[clone trooper]] [[Tup]] [[Death|executed]] Tiplar by shooting her in the head due to a malfunction in his [[Behavioral modification biochip|inhibitor chip]], which triggered a premature activation of [[Order 66|Clone Protocol 66]], a [[Sith]]-implanted directive that branded all Jedi as [[Treason|traitors]]. Tiplar's death cost the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] forces a potential victory and instead forced them to retreat, while Tup's apparent act of [[treason]] sparked a high-profile investigation that led [[Advanced Recon Commando|ARC trooper]] [[Fives]] to uncover the existence and function of the [[Cloning|clones']] inhibitor chips.

==Biography==
===Casualty of the Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Good soldiers follow orders.|Tup, just before gunning down Tiplar|<ref name="The Unknown" />}}
Tiplar, a [[Mikkian]] [[Gender|female]], lived during the final [[Standard decade|decades]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]. She and her [[twin]] sister, [[Tiplee]], were both [[Force-sensitive]] and were inducted into the [[Jedi Order]]<ref name="The Unknown" /> in a rare example of [[Jedi]] who were not totally separated from their prior family with their induction.<ref name="Uncommon Bond">{{SW|url=news/twins-in-star-wars|text=An Uncommon Bond: Twins in ''Star Wars'' Stories}}</ref> Both of them eventually attained the rank of [[Jedi Master]]. Following the [[First Battle of Geonosis|outbreak]] of the [[Clone Wars]], Tiplar and her sister accepted commissions as [[Jedi General]]s in the [[Grand Army of the Republic]],<ref name="The Unknown" /> and they sometimes served together<ref name="Databank" /> in military campaigns against the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="The Unknown" /> They frequently fought alongside [[clone trooper]]s under the command of [[Clone Commander]] [[Doom]].<ref name="Databank: Doom">{{Databank|clone-commander-doom|Clone Commander Doom}}</ref>

[[File:Force_Speed_2018_SWD_Store_Championship_alt_card.png|thumb|left|250px|Tiplar and Tiplee lead the Republic's advance during the Battle of Ringo Vinda.]]
In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> Tiplar joined forces with Tiplee, Doom, and [[Jedi]] [[General]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] to repel a Confederate battle group from an [[orbit]]al [[Ringo Vinda space station|space station]] that encircled the [[planet]] [[Ringo Vinda]]. The ensuing [[Battle of Ringo Vinda|campaign]] lasted several [[Standard day|rotations]], leading to a stalemate between the Republic and Confederate forces. Determined to break the deadlock, Tiplar and her comrades launched an offensive against the [[battle droid]] [[infantry]] led by Confederate [[Admiral]] [[Trench]], advancing through the [[space station]]'s corridors in an attempt to reach<ref name="The Unknown" /> a communications center.<ref name="The Unknown Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-unknown-episode-guide|text="The Unknown" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> Upon encountering a [[squad]] of [[BX-series droid commando]]s, Tiplar ordered Doom and his [[Cloning|clone]] [[soldier]]s to shore up their left flank against the incoming [[droid]]s. The appearance of a trio of [[droideka]]s led Tiplar to have her men prop up their energy shields, which they used to repel the droideka's heavy barrages of [[Laser|blasterfire]]. Reaching out with [[the Force]], Tiplar [[Telekinesis|telekinetically]] pushed the droidekas off their footing long enough for Doom and his soldiers to roll [[Electromagnetic pulse grenade|Electro Magnetic Pulse grenades]] underneath the droids' shields, thus disabling their adversaries. They proceeded to the communications center, where they eliminated the droids manning the station.<ref name="The Unknown" />

Once they had secured their position, Tiplar and Tiplee met with Skywalker and his [[troop]]s from the [[501st Legion]] to coordinate their assault on Trench's command center. Trench had requested reinforcements, so it was imperative that they capture the enemy facility as soon as possible. Since there were three hallways that led to the command center, Skywalker suggested that each Jedi General take one of the corridors; their teams would converge on Trench's position at the same [[time]], thereby overwhelming his defenses. Skywalker had [[Advanced Recon Commando|ARC trooper]] [[Fives]] and 501st [[trooper]] [[Tup]] bring along ten of their best soldiers to supplement Tiplar and Doom's men, who had been severely depleted in the earlier assault.<ref name="The Unknown" />

With their plan in place, Tiplar and Doom proceeded to the left passageway with Fives, Tup, and their troops and marched through the corridor, demolishing all of the droid forces that they encountered. Tiplar and her troopers soon reached the spacious chamber in front of Trench's command center, where they used some stacks of crates as cover from Trench's [[B1-series battle droid]]s, [[DSD1 dwarf spider droid]]s,<ref name="The Unknown" /> and [[Super battle droid rocket trooper|B2 super rocket troopers]].<ref name="The Unknown Guide" /> However, just as the Republic forces were on the verge of conquering Trench's infantry,<ref name="The Unknown" /> a malfunction in Tup's [[Behavioral modification biochip|inhibitor chip]] caused him to prematurely execute [[Order 66|Clone Protocol 66]], a [[Sith]]-engineered command to execute all Jedi as traitors.<ref name="Conspiracy">{{TCW|Conspiracy}}</ref><ref name="Fugitive">{{TCW|Fugitive}}</ref> As Tiplar was deflecting incoming enemy [[blaster]]fire with her [[lightsaber]], Tup strode over to her, and when she turned towards him in surprise, he shot her in the face with his [[DC-15A blaster carbine]], instantly killing her.<ref name="The Unknown" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|Why? Why would he do this?''"<br />"''I'm about to find out.|Tiplee and Anakin Skywalker, proceeding with Tup's interrogation following his murder of Tiplar|<ref name="The Unknown" />}}
[[File:PrematureExecution-TU.png|thumb|right|250px|Tup's mid-battle execution of Tiplar was the result of a premature activation of Clone Protocol 66.]]
Tiplar's death impeded the Republic's advance, turning an imminent victory into a retreat. Tiplee was shocked to witness Tiplar's execution and mourned her late sister. Tiplar's comrades brought her body back to the communications center, where Skywalker and 501st [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]] interrogated Tup regarding his apparent act of [[treason]]. However, Tup merely repeated the phrase "Good soldiers follow orders" before unsuccessfully attacking Tiplee. Meanwhile, news of Tiplar's death reached Separatist leader [[Count]] [[Dooku]], who ordered Trench to retrieve Tup for analysis. Trench's efforts failed,<ref name="The Unknown" /> and Fives and Rex escorted Tup back to the clone [[homeworld]] of [[Kamino]], where Jedi Master [[Shaak Ti]] and [[Kaminoan]] [[Chief Medical Scientist]] [[Nala Se]] subjected Tup to medical examination to uncover the source of his breakdown.<ref name="Conspiracy" />

Ultimately, Fives learned of the Sith's conspiracy against the Jedi and the machinations leading to Tiplar's murder,<ref name="Fugitive" /> but he was [[Mission to Level 1325|killed]] before he could prove his findings to the Jedi. The [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] [[Darth Sidious]], in his guise as [[Supreme Chancellor]] Sheev Palpatine, provided the Republic's official explanation that a Ringo Vindan [[parasite]] had led Tup's inhibitor chip&mdash;supposedly there to keep the clones mentally stable&mdash;to deteriorate, thus causing his execution of Tiplar. The same excuse was used to discredit Fives and "explain" the actions he had taken while attempting to reveal the truth.<ref name="Orders">{{TCW|Orders (episode)}}</ref>

[[File:AdiGalliaTCWYoda.png|thumb|left|250px|Tiplar appeared in Yoda's vision alongside other deceased Jedi.]]
Toward the end of the Clone Wars,<ref name="Databank: Moraband">{{Databank|moraband|Moraband}}</ref> Jedi [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] traveled to a [[Wellspring of Life|planet]] that was the birthplace of the [[midi-chlorian]]s. There, five [[Force Priestesses]] subjected him to a series of trials to determine whether he was worthy of learning the knowledge they possessed. In the [[Valley of Extinction]], Yoda saw a [[Force vision|vision]] of the [[Jedi Temple training ground]], where Tiplar and a number of other Jedi, alive and dead, appeared as they had before the war. Though tempted to join his colleagues, Yoda recognized the impossibility of the illusion and overcame it, bringing the vision to an end.<ref name="Destiny">{{TCW|Destiny (The Clone Wars)}}</ref>

After the [[Skirmish aboard the Tribunal|issuing]] of Order 66, former [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] and her [[astromech droid]] [[R7-A7]] found files about Tiplar and her death at Tup's hands while reading secure files on Fives to ascertain what was wrong with the clones onboard the [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyer]]<ref name="Shattered">{{TCW|Shattered}}</ref> ''[[Tribunal]]'',<ref name="Join the Battle" /> following up on a clue Rex had managed to give her before his control chip took him over. The files included images of Tiplar and Tup, a [[brain]] scan showing the location of the chip, a report from Nala Se listing the official explanation for Tup's actions, and a grievance report Rex had filed after Fives' death reporting his suspicions that the chips might have an ulterior purpose. Tano, R7, and two other droids were then able to capture Rex and remove his chip, restoring his free will.<ref name="Shattered" /> The two of them subsequently escaped the [[Star Destroyer]] before it crashed, killing everyone still onboard.<ref name="Victory and Death">{{TCW|Victory and Death}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Shields up!''"<br />"''Yes, sir!|Tiplar and her soldiers react to the deployment of droidekas during the Battle of Ringo Vinda|<ref name="The Unknown" />}}
[[File:Tiplar_and_Doom_marines.png|thumb|right|240px|Tiplar and Doom collaborated in campaigns during the Clone Wars.]]
A Mikkian female, Tiplar stood at 1.8 [[meter]]s (5 [[Foot|feet]], 11 inches) tall<ref name="Join the Battle" /> and had [[Color|yellow-green]] skin and blue [[eye]]s. Her forehead was adorned with a [[tattoo]]<ref name="Databank" /> that was identical to that of her twin sister, Tiplee. Tiplar formed a good working relationship with [[Commander]] Doom and the soldiers under her command, and they worked together to efficiently eliminate threats on the battlefield, summarily disabling BX-series droid [[commando]]s as well as droidekas during<ref name="The Unknown" /> the Battle of Ringo Vinda.<ref name="Databank: Doom" /> She was also known to for skills as a leader and was proficient at military tactics.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Powers and abilities==
An accomplished and experienced field general,<ref name="SWCT Tiplar">{{Topps|set=2020 Topps Women of Star Wars|cardname=#90: Tiplar|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/216003/cid/14374583/2020-Topps-Women-of-Star-Wars-90-Tiplar|nobackup=1}}</ref> Tiplar possessed a mastery of the Force and consequently achieved the rank of Jedi Master. She was adept with telekinesis, evinced during the Battle of Ringo Vinda when she pushed a trio of enemy droidekas off their footing long enough for her clone troopers to dispatch them. She was also agile, and she used that in conjunction with skill with a lightsaber to deflect incoming blaster bolts and execute acrobatic flips on the battlefield.<ref name="The Unknown" /> On top of her armed combat skills, she was also proficient at unarmed combat.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Equipment==
Tiplar wielded a [[Tiplar's lightsaber|green-bladed lightsaber]] in combat. Her [[Clothing|apparel]] consisted of a full-body outfit, [[boot]]s, and a headpiece.<ref name="The Unknown" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Female_Sith_Concept_Art.png|thumb|right|150px|Tiplar and Tiplee were based on concept art by Iain McCaig.]]
The character of Tiplar was created for the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series and debuted in the episode "[[The Unknown]]."<ref name="The Unknown Guide" /> The episode was released as part of [[The Clone Wars: The Lost Missions|The Lost Missions]], the series' sixth season, on [[March 7]], [[2014]].<ref name="Lost Missions on Netflix">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-the-lost-missions-now-on-netflix|text=Star Wars: The Clone Wars &ndash; The Lost Missions Now on Netflix|nolive=1}}</ref> On [[March 11]], [[2013]], almost a year prior to the episode's release, Tiplar was featured in a promotional clip for the series.<ref name="A New Direction">{{SW|url=news/a-new-direction-for-lucasfilm-animation|text=A New Direction for Lucasfilm Animation}} {{C|Promotional clip removed after article's release}}</ref> Both Tiplar and her sister, Tiplee, were portrayed by voice actor [[Anna Graves]],<ref name="The Unknown" /> who also voiced other recurring characters throughout the series like [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]] and the [[bounty hunter]] [[Sugi (bounty hunter)|Sugi]].<ref name="The Mandalore Plot">{{TCW|The Mandalore Plot}}</ref><ref name="Bounty Hunters">{{TCW|Bounty Hunters (episode)}}</ref> Although "The Unknown" depicts Tiplar as being killed by being shot in the face, as she turns in surprise when Tup walks up to her, her face has no markings on it when Tiplee picks up her body.<ref name="The Unknown" />

Tiplar's and Tiplee's character models were based on unused concept art for a female [[Sith]] that [[Iain McCaig]] created for the film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']].<ref name="The Unknown Guide" /> Caig designed multiple images of "[[Wikipedia:Medusa|Medusa]]-like" figures<ref name="Art of AotC">''[[The Art of Star Wars Episode II: Attack of the Clones]]''</ref> that would later evolve into the Mikkians;<ref name="The Unknown trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-unknown-trivia-gallery|text=The Unknown Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Silde 3}}</ref> one of which had yellow skin and a headpiece <ref name="Art of AotC" /> close to Tiplar's.<ref name="The Unknown" />

''[[Star Wars Jedi Pocket Expert]]'' mistakenly states that Tiplar was a [[Jedi Knight]].<ref name="Pocket Expert">''[[Star Wars Jedi Pocket Expert]]''</ref>

